---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Get started | Krabka"
  description="Evaluate Krabka with a local quickstart, browser experiments, compatibility checks, measured benchmarks, and an isolated staging cluster."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-left border-b border-white/10 pb-8 mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
        Get started with Krabka
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-300">
        Try Krabka with your Kafka applications, or explore it in your browser. Choose a starting point below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div id="evaluation-pathways" class="mb-14">
      <div id="first-run-options" class="grid items-stretch gap-6 lg:grid-cols-5">
        <section class="frosted-card flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 p-6 lg:col-span-3" aria-labelledby="local-validation">
          <h2 id="local-validation" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Local and CI validation</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Run a local broker with the quickstart, then produce and consume your first records. Point your existing Kafka clients, kcat, or integration tests at <code>localhost:9092</code>, and repeat those checks in CI as your application changes.</p>
          <div class="mt-auto pt-6">
            <a href={getPath('/docs/quickstart')} class="inline-block rounded-lg bg-krab-600 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-krab-500">Run the local quickstart</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <aside class="frosted-card flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 p-6 lg:col-span-2" aria-labelledby="browser-trial">
          <h2 id="browser-trial" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Interactive sandbox</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Try Cluster Lab in your browser without a local installation. Explore KRaft consensus, replica failover, and fault injection with WebAssembly brokers.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400"><span id="lab-phone-limit" class="min-[700px]:hidden">View-only on phones. </span><span id="lab-scope-limit">The simulation does not measure production throughput or disk durability.</span></p>
          <div class="mt-auto pt-6">
            <a href={getPath('/docs/lab/')} class="inline-block rounded-lg border border-krab-500 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-krab-400 hover:bg-krab-500/10">Open Cluster Lab</a>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div id="evaluation-depth" class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Evaluate in depth</h2>
        <section id="compatibility" class="grid items-start gap-3 border-b border-white/10 py-6 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:gap-6" aria-labelledby="preflight-check">
          <h3 id="preflight-check" class="text-xl font-bold text-white lg:col-span-2">Preflight compatibility and parity check</h3>
          <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-3">
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Check your clients, <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/kip_matrix')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Kafka APIs</a>, <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/operations/migrate-from-kafka#cut-the-schema-registry-over')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">schema registry workflow</a>, and <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/operations/ecosystem-support#what-does-not-work')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">tooling limitations</a> before a broader trial; Krabka serves no JMX and loads no JVM plugins. Use evidence for your intended release; results from another revision do not establish support for your build.</p>
            <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/operations/support-matrix')} class="mt-3 inline-block text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Check the support matrix</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="grid items-start gap-3 border-b border-white/10 py-6 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:gap-6" aria-labelledby="performance-evaluation">
          <h3 id="performance-evaluation" class="text-xl font-bold text-white lg:col-span-2">Check performance for your workload</h3>
          <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-3">
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Compare measured throughput, latency, and CPU use for workloads relevant to your application. Review the test conditions and limits; published results do not promise the same performance for your workload.</p>
            <a href={getPath('/benchmarks')} class="mt-3 inline-block text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Explore the benchmarks</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="grid items-start gap-3 border-b border-white/10 py-6 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:gap-6" aria-labelledby="staging-evaluation">
          <h3 id="staging-evaluation" class="text-xl font-bold text-white lg:col-span-2">Non-disruptive staging evaluation</h3>
          <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-3">
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Evaluate representative traffic on an isolated Krabka cluster while production clients stay on Kafka. Use the migration guide to compare application behavior and results with dual writes, MirrorMaker 2 replication, or shadow consumers, and review their limitations, precautions, and consumer offsets before you plan a cutover.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400">For a disposable Kubernetes cluster, follow the <a href={getPath('/docs/kubernetes-quickstart')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Kubernetes quickstart</a>.</p>
            <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/operations/migrate-from-kafka')} class="mt-3 inline-block text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Plan a staging evaluation</a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="grid items-start gap-3 border-b border-white/10 py-6 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:gap-6" aria-labelledby="explore-verification">
          <h3 id="explore-verification" class="text-xl font-bold text-white lg:col-span-2">How Krabka is verified</h3>
          <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-3">
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Explore the evidence behind Krabka's correctness claims, including formal proofs, model checking, and testing. The verification overview explains what each approach covers and where its limits lie.</p>
            <a href={getPath('/verification')} class="mt-3 inline-block text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Explore verification</a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p id="clients" class="text-sm text-gray-300">The application examples are in the <a href={getPath('/docs/quickstart#clients')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">local quickstart: connect your application</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
